// array_add to a resizable array whose allocated says its memory has room
// but whose data is null (issue #158, spec 3.17, 8.4): its count is below
// allocated, so the add wouldn't grow it and would write its item through
// null. Its data is checked with the count and allocated, and the program
// stops at the built-in's name.
main :: () {
    a : [..]int;
    a.allocated = 4;
    array_add(*a, 1);
}
